+{"id":"da6dabf0-7766-4006-9661-ad8d1f139e74","timestamp":"2026-11-11T08:20:02.566562","source":"environment","parent_id":"bbfc0af7-30a9-4629-a7e9-e684b6ed42b0","tool_name":"file_editor","tool_call_id":"call_eb1863891f704cb682bf3204","observation":{"content":[{"cache_prompt":false,"type":"text","text":"Here's the result of running `cat -n` on /workspace/record/record.py:\n     1\t#!/usr/bin/env python3\n     2\t\"\"\"exagium record: an append-only, hash-chained ledger of plans and verdicts, with outside anchors.\n     3\t\n     4\tLayout (under --ledger, default ../ledger):\n     5\t  entries/000001.json ...   one entry per file; CI (.github/workflows/record.yml) is the only writer\n     6\t  anchors/NNNNNN.sigstore.json   Sigstore attestation by the writer of the range of entries it added, ending at NNNNNN\n     7\t  anchors/NNNNNN.ots             OpenTimestamps proof of entry NNNNNN's bytes\n     8\t  inbox/*.json                   proposals {\"kind\": ..., \"body\": ...}; CI moves them into entries/\n     9\t\n    10\tAn entry's identity is the sha256 of its stored bytes, which must be exactly its RFC 8785 (JCS) form\n    11\t(no trailing newline). The rules that make Python's json.dumps output equal JCS are enforced: ASCII\n    12\tkeys, no floats, integers within +-(2**53-1), no lone surrogates.\n    13\t\n    14\tCommands: ingest | verify | head | range | check-anchors | monitor.\n    15\tExit codes: 0 ok; 1 the ledger, an anchor or the monitor's finding is wrong; 2 can't check (missing\n    16\tlibrary or network); 3 unexpected failure. A failure is never reported as a verdict.\n    17\t\"\"\"\n    18\timport argparse, base64, datetime, hashlib, json, os, re, subprocess, sys, urllib.error, urllib.request\n    19\t\n    20\tMAX_INT = 2**53 - 1\n    21\tKINDS = (\"plan\", \"verdict\", \"orphan\")\n    22\tOUTCOMES = (\"pass\", \"fail\", \"inconclusive\")\n    23\tHEX64 = re.compile(r\"[0-9a-f]{64}\")\n    24\tNAME = re.compile(r\"[a-z0-9][a-z0-9._-]{0,63}\")  #