    ...\n    if covered < len(chain):\n        bad.append(...)\n    max_pending = getattr(a, \"max_pending_hours\", None)\n    if max_pending is not None:\n        now = datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc)\n        for seq in sorted(pending):\n            t = att_at.get(seq)\n            if t is None:\n                continue\n            hours = int((now - datetime.datetime.fromtimestamp(t, datetime.timezone.utc)).total_seconds() // 3600)\n            if hours > max_pending:\n                bad.append(f\"anchors/{seq:06d}.ots is still pending {hours} h\")\n    print(...)\n```\n\nWait, ordering: bad list order affects messages; put pending check before printing. Fine.\n\nHmm — one subtlety: `sorted(ranges)` sorts 3-tuples, fine.\n\nAnother subtlety: the pending bad message: should it include anchor name? \"Print to stderr a message containing `still pending N h`\". `f\"anchors/{seq:06d}.ots is still pending {hours} h\"` contains \"still pending 72 h\". Good.\n\nNow argparse:\n\n```python\nif name == \"check-anchors\":\n    p.add_argument(\"--ref\", default=\"refs/heads/main\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--explorer\", action=\"append\", default=None, help=...)\n    p.add_argument(\"--max-pending-hours\", type=int, default=None, metavar=\"H\",\n                   help=\"exit 1 if a pending OpenTimestamps proof is older than H hours (pending means not yet confirmed in Bitcoin)\")\n```\n\nargparse converts `--max-pending-hours` to `max_pending_hours`. Good.\n\nShould H be validated positive? type=int; maybe allow 0. Keep simple.\n\nNow, should the pending check also apply when the ots proof is pending but there's no sigstore anchor? Skip.\n\nAlso: should we only flag the *first* stale pending or all? \"if any range head's proof is still pending and its ... time is more than H hours ago, exit 1. Print to stderr a message containing still pending N h\". Printing all stale ones is fine; message contains the pattern.\n\nHmm, but maybe better to print one message per stale pending proof. With multiple pending, multiple messages each containing \"still pending N h\". Fine.\n\nWait, one more consideration: should the check use hours > max_pending, or >= ? \"more than H hours ago\" → hours > H. \"A pending proof younger than H hours is fine\" → hours <= H fine. With H=0 and pending just now, hours=0, 0 > 0 false → fine. Good.\n\nNow also consider: maybe instead of tracking pending list, check inside loop. But pending list is cleaner.\n\nOne issue: `pending` set vs list — list of seqs. An anchor file could exist only as ots (pending). Could two pending? Just use list.\n\nAlso should the JSON \"wrong\" include this? It's fine.\n\nHmm, actually wait. Let me reconsider whether to add to `bad` or print separately. If added to bad, the JSON report includes it and the \"BAD: \" prefix prints to stderr. The stderr message would be like `BAD: anchors/000002.ots is still pending 72 h`. Contains required substring. OK.\n\nBut hmm — \"exit 1\" required. bad → exit 1. Good. And without option, no additions → unchanged behavior (exit 0 for pending-only).\n\nNow the docstring of cmd_check_anchors should maybe be updated. Minor.\n\nLet's also double check `iso` and time handling: `t` from check_sigstore is int integratedTime; `datetime.datetime.fromtimestamp(t, datetime.timezone.utc)`.\n\nNow write the edits.","thinking_blocks":[],"action":{"command":"str_replace","path":"/workspace/record/record.py","view_range":[383,390],"kind":"FileEditorAction"},"tool_name":"file_editor","tool_call_id":"call_0ec00e101ce9483fbb23ee66","tool_call":{"id":"call_0ec00e101ce9483fbb23ee66","name":"file_editor","arguments":"{\"command\": \"str_replace\", \"path\": \"/workspace/record/record.py\", \"view_range\": [383, 390]}","origin":"completion"},"llm_response_id":"gen-1794385271-JV0NhsvKZ3CvYaXSfksi","security_risk":"UNKNOWN","summary":"file_editor: {\"command\": \"str_replace\", \"path\": \"/workspace/record/record.py\", \"view_range\": [383, 390]}","kind":"ActionEv